[613]={["atomIDs"]={"613:description:1-7","613:description:10-69","613:description:72-126","613:description:131-171","613:description:174-256","613:description:259-380","613:description:383-417","613:description:422-499","613:objective:1-55"},["opening"]="Maury's recovered foot concealed loot behind a lock MacKinley could not open. Maury's history of gambling with the Mosh'Ogg, and being chased away after winning, suggested the ogres might hold its key.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to find Maury's Key for MacKinley.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Maury's Key to Sea Wolf MacKinley.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="e1645dd2217677b3821a70dc0e9bb08dc28f5e329ff0d818de146b1626b65c20",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[614]={["atomIDs"]={"614:description:1-68","614:description:71-124","614:description:129-136","614:description:141-174","614:description:177-252","614:description:255-311","614:description:314-349","614:description:352-361","614:description:366-411","614:description:414-444","614:description:447-500","614:objective:1-54"},["opening"]="Smotts described losing his ship and crew to sea giants, then being sent back to Booty Bay in a lifeboat. Gorlash had taken the captain's chest for a snuffbox and reportedly roamed the eastern coast.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover Smotts' Chest from Gorlash.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned Smotts' Chest to Hecklebury Smotts.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="40ae448330e511e1b62c3c92426e7013120e8aa4e3cbb17c5f62f89d96cf85f1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[615]={["atomIDs"]={"615:description:1-61","615:description:64-155","615:description:158-190","615:description:193-275","615:description:280-339","615:description:344-381","615:description:386-405","615:description:408-475","615:description:478-508","615:objective:1-20"},["opening"]="Smotts' second ship had fared no better than his first attempt against the giants. Negolash now held his cutlass; the surviving cook Sprogger was the suggested guide to finding him.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to ask Sprogger about Negolash.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Sprogger about the giant and the missing cutlass.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="77d3b1720361482e8b9391d2280db35457d4fdf0f88367eec3c1422b8968eb4e",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[616]={["atomIDs"]={"616:description:1-116","616:description:118-250","616:description:252-304","616:description:309-382","616:objective:1-39"},["opening"]="Krazek passed on a sailors' ghost story gathered for Revilgaz. They spoke of a haunted island with water elementals and a raving goblin apparition, a report odd enough to interest the baron.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to relay the island rumor to Revilgaz.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Baron Revilgaz about the haunted-island report.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="10c275e280e70d1e3ba973138394ee60ba8f2127438907020e5d72dd6a80afa7",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[617]={["atomIDs"]={"617:description:1-25","617:description:27-80","617:description:85-208","617:description:210-279","617:description:284-350","617:description:352-412","617:objective:1-65"},["opening"]="Bloads had a buyer for akiris reed, though he did not know its use. Naga along the northern beach carried the ocean plant, and ten bundles would make a profitable shipment.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather ten Bundles of Akiris Reed for Bloads.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered ten Bundles of Akiris Reed to Privateer Bloads.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="8c7ca54b3743b1298554d8a09c742968c839e97409a0826692e05c592698b402",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[618]={["atomIDs"]={"618:description:1-27","618:description:32-105","618:description:108-155","618:description:158-211","618:description:214-294","618:description:299-376","618:description:379-442","618:description:445-500","618:objective:1-94","618:objective:99-174"},["opening"]="Sprogger remembered Negolash heading for the ship's kitchen instead of its crew. Wine and his special buzzard wings might lure the giant to the old lifeboat, where Smotts' stolen cutlass could be sought.",["pending"]="{actor} would prepare the wine-and-wings lure, confront Negolash and return Smotts' Cutlass.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Negolash lure assignment and delivered Smotts' Cutlass to the captain.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="ed369d31d9627501c096f55b389a943f887b84b9c879235a91e36d9c18466770",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[621]={["atomIDs"]={"621:description:1-101","621:description:104-131","621:description:134-137","621:description:139-145","621:description:150-225","621:description:228-330","621:description:335-402","621:description:407-470","621:objective:1-69"},["opening"]="Crank described Zanzil's plant mixture as a means to suppress followers' wills while strengthening their bodies. Rather than destroy that knowledge, he wanted twelve samples from the outcast's ruined settlements for uses of his own.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to obtain twelve samples of Zanzil's Mixture for Crank.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered twelve samples of Zanzil's Mixture to Crank Fizzlebub.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="6a52929e177f2e4968ab2f8f5ed9022c94bf8c665e99ee08041db7a8c4bb19ea",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[622]={["atomIDs"]={"622:description:1-51","622:description:54-99","622:description:102-167","622:description:172-222","622:description:225-261","622:objective:1-61"},["opening"]="Krazek had repaired the rebels' pot and added a steam whistle and a bone-cutting chopper. The finished utensil was ready to return to Corporal Kaleb.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to deliver Krazek's Fixed Pot to Kaleb.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Krazek's Fixed Pot to Corporal Kaleb.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="a5bb55d010d1b72d0b68b33856970cb9c378b14177e1f7a00fe06dc0d0a712c8",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[623]={["atomIDs"]={"623:description:1-73","623:description:75-201","623:description:206-342","623:description:347-366","623:description:368-413","623:description:415-498","623:objective:1-62"},["bridge"]="The reed collection had reached Bloads just as Groy requested another shipment. A waiting Theramore client made an earlier delivery useful before Bloads's own voyage the following week.",["bridgeFrom"]=617,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Groy had requested more akiris for a waiting client, but Bloads would not sail for a week. He offered a traveler the chance to carry the bundle to Theramore sooner.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to deliver the Bundle of Akiris Reeds to Groy.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Bundle of Akiris Reeds to Privateer Groy in Theramore.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="381aedd4059c5698b643fdbd9afbcebad48a19180413b1eb3f99c354ae463e12",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[624]={["atomIDs"]={"624:description:1-40","624:description:43-80","624:description:83-122","624:description:125-158","624:description:161-199","624:description:202-240","624:objective:1-17"},["opening"]="Cortello's verse sent its reader toward a bridge in the Swamp of Sorrows. Beneath that crossing, east of Deadwind and south of Redridge, the riddle promised another clue.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to solve the bridge riddle in the Swamp of Sorrows.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the first stage of Cortello's riddle.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="06bec8f6a1614a476e728c138b1458cc100d5347d8c4139dd57340c6fb2b7e78",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[625]={["atomIDs"]={"625:description:1-33","625:description:36-73","625:description:76-111","625:description:114-151","625:description:154-199","625:description:202-247","625:objective:1-17"},["opening"]="The next verse carried the search across the sea to Dustwallow. A cave in the marsh's southwest was the promised location of another clue amid the danger east of the Barrens.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to solve the Dustwallow cave riddle.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Dustwallow stage of Cortello's riddle.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="2fc3b8d74cdf171e41f78d86751ffd4083be81394d05ea6c77618039c4d2027d",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[626]={["atomIDs"]={"626:description:1-13","626:description:15-39","626:description:42-80","626:description:83-120","626:description:123-163","626:description:166-231","626:description:234-284","626:objective:1-17"},["opening"]="Cortello's final directions returned to Lordaeron and the Hinterlands coast. The promised treasure lay beneath the water at the foot of the great falls.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to solve the riddle at the Hinterlands falls.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the final stage of Cortello's riddle.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="42a078f5df2690a4923d5465551189097dbde59156396b9db6ca6036a2340b10",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[627]={["atomIDs"]={"627:description:1-87","627:description:90-126","627:description:129-231","627:description:233-270","627:description:275-292","627:description:297-348","627:description:350-380","627:description:383-430","627:description:435-483","627:description:485-506","627:objective:1-62"},["opening"]="Krazek agreed to repair the pot while his customer fetched another commodity. Lesser Bloodstone Ore from far-off Drywhisker Gorge remained valuable to those who knew its uses, and he wanted four loads.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to obtain four loads of Lesser Bloodstone Ore for Krazek.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered four loads of Lesser Bloodstone Ore to Krazek.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="1e0d4b6f9e804d5842473f1d8ece06495c4cf6c09487e420a09f3d9c005a5e76",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[628]={["aftermath"]="Drizzlik expected to send Riddlevox's order on the next boat to Undermine, ahead of schedule. The three kinds of crocolisk leather had brought the boots to that point.",["atomIDs"]={"628:description:1-68","628:description:70-116","628:description:118-244","628:description:249-367","628:description:369-478","628:objective:1-55"},["bridge"]="The boots' inner layers had their leather. Drizzlik now sought the outer surface that would carry his designs: a perfect skin from an elder saltwater crocolisk.",["bridgeFrom"]=577,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"628:completion:1-6","628:completion:8-120","628:completion:122-145","628:completion:150-214","628:completion:216-232","628:completion:237-310"},["opening"]="The Excelsior boots' inner work was finished, leaving the visible layer. Drizzlik required an elder saltwater crocolisk's skin for durability and decoration, warning that an elder might emerge only to defend its kin.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to obtain an Elder Crocolisk Skin for Drizzlik.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered an Elder Crocolisk Skin to Drizzlik.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="45cacc1d6b122d285fb393afe8f3868f120cbafc019828193b04b7c1d0fb7728",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[629]={["atomIDs"]={"629:description:1-118","629:description:121-232","629:description:237-341","629:description:344-494","629:objective:1-61"},["opening"]="A sunken city in the Vile Reef preserved a tablet telling Gri'lek's sacred tale. Too large to move whole, it could still yield a shard for the Darkspears' new home in Orgrimmar, if the murlocs allowed the approach.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover a Tablet Shard from the Vile Reef for Kin'weelay.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered a Tablet Shard to Kin'weelay.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="2e165d64a12e0b296a3537176212d9f119ca3911e244f6e41cc8624b5ffa0dcc",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[630]={["aftermath"]="Poobah regarded her rescue as deliverance from dishonor. She wished she could offer a place among her tribe but did not claim the authority to do so.",["atomIDs"]={"630:description:1-68","630:description:70-111","630:description:113-216","630:description:218-306","630:description:311-416","630:objective:1-71"},["bridge"]="The bottled plea had led to Poobah. She named King Mukla as her captor and called for his shackle key, giving the island search its direct rescue objective.",["bridgeFrom"]=594,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"630:completion:1-44","630:completion:46-113","630:completion:115-210"},["opening"]="Poobah named King Mukla as the Skymane keeping her chained on the island. His command over its beasts left her captive, and the key to her shackle had to be recovered from him.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront King Mukla and return the shackle key to Poobah.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the King Mukla assignment and returned the key to Princess Poobah.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="64bda1913bd046aa9b8dae22bf41e1e5338711c0c7d3e208b6c43d48f1d18aab",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[631]={["atomIDs"]={"631:description:1-48","631:description:51-77","631:description:82-127","631:description:130-209","631:description:214-289","631:description:292-377","631:description:382-399","631:description:402-469","631:description:474-500","631:objective:1-48"},["opening"]="Rhag recalled the explosion that shattered the span and killed its defenders. Rustlocke went to scout the eastern bridge days ago, but the siege of Dun Modr had left no soldiers free to search for him.",["pending"]="{actor} would locate Ol' Rustlocke near the Thandol Span.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} located Ol' Rustlocke.",["sourceHash"]="e5f345727d9816cffbe80e75eec7836ce9f575d5bd7ad82911cd5251a1a04137",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[632]={["atomIDs"]={"632:description:1-66","632:description:69-117","632:description:122-187","632:objective:1-88"},["opening"]="Rustlocke appeared to have fallen in a Dark Iron ambush. A parchment beside his clenched fist might explain what he found, and Rhag had to receive both it and the news.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take Rustlocke's parchment and the grim report to Rhag.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported Rustlocke's fate to Rhag Garmason and delivered the parchment.",["sourceHash"]="b3d7813881d022bbcbfe6dd727e6eb64d6dd4fc0143c92d121bb70bc844b1d7a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[633]={["aftermath"]="Rhag declared the remaining bridge saved. His relief still depended on holding out for reinforcements that had not yet arrived.",["atomIDs"]={"633:description:1-11","633:description:14-28","633:description:31-58","633:description:63-101","633:description:104-304","633:description:309-402","633:description:405-436","633:description:439-481","633:description:486-506","633:objective:1-32"},["bridge"]="Rustlocke's parchment had reached Rhag with the news of his death. It named Kam Deepfury's explosives cache across the span; destroying that store could keep the remaining bridge from following the first.",["bridgeFrom"]=632,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"633:completion:1-30","633:completion:32-104","633:completion:109-177"},["opening"]="Rustlocke's parchment named Kam Deepfury and an explosives cache across the span in Arathi. Rhag feared the remaining bridge and northern supply line would be lost if that cache reached its target.",["pending"]="{actor} would destroy the explosives cache across the Thandol Span.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment to destroy the explosives cache and returned to Rhag.",["sourceHash"]="cf92ea424f5d8bc8a9cf28f5e686b906050b1bb826d5918bd4d4bd0524580be0",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[634]={["aftermath"]="Nials offered sympathy but no troops. Stromgarde's own fall bound the Refuge Pointe force to reclaiming its city, leaving Longbraid to face his position without their help.",["atomIDs"]={"634:description:1-38","634:description:41-75","634:description:78-176","634:description:181-220","634:description:223-332","634:objective:1-40"},["bridge"]="The cache assignment had ended, but the defenders still needed relief. Rhag appealed northward to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe, hoping the Alliance force could spare troops for Dun Modr and the span.",["bridgeFrom"]=633,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"634:completion:1-58","634:completion:60-145","634:completion:150-175","634:completion:177-217","634:completion:219-264","634:completion:269-391","634:completion:393-446"},["opening"]="Ironforge's reserves had still not arrived. Rhag turned north to the Alliance camp at Refuge Pointe, hoping Captain Nials could spare soldiers for Dun Modr and the span.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to seek Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe with Rhag's appeal.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe.",["sourceHash"]="4e358cb5dbbb14b87dca47f1a549b4bc7b2d4fed31f9e9f6cc462108a234c85c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[635]={["aftermath"]="Its pulse suggested a living presence confined within it.",["atomIDs"]={"635:description:1-35","635:description:40-171","635:description:176-300","635:description:305-333","635:objective:1-34"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"635:completion:1-63"},["opening"]="The shard pulsed with what seemed a plea for help. A vision pointed toward Arathi's northern mountains and a brilliant crystal rising from the earth there.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to seek the crystal shown in the vision.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} found the mountain crystal.",["sourceHash"]="60c6bcdcd43c79b3123e0833a80ac8f9b982e09a55659f8fbc034d9efef5056e",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[637]={["aftermath"]="Sara asked to read Sully's letter, refusing at first to accept the report of him beneath the water. The response preserved her immediate grief rather than inventing its resolution.",["atomIDs"]={"637:description:1-149","637:description:154-186","637:description:188-242","637:objective:1-45"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"637:completion:1-55","637:completion:57-72","637:completion:77-105"},["opening"]="A damaged envelope dissolved around a carefully written letter. The surviving pages still named Sara Balloo of Ironforge, preserving an address after war and water had nearly erased the message.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to deliver Sully Balloo's Letter to Sara.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Sully Balloo's Letter to Sara Balloo.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="a1e92517f7d045907b359ead31f88d21261617971c93dc52dd1cc716df57e06a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[638]={["aftermath"]="Zengu welcomed the assistance while stressing the difficulty of Vol'jin's task. The meeting arranged help for the sword's recovery rather than recovering it itself.",["atomIDs"]={"638:description:1-244","638:description:249-373","638:objective:1-66"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"638:completion:1-18","638:completion:20-149"},["opening"]="Vol'jin sought the sword Trol'kalar after Thoras Trollbane's death and Stromgarde's ruin. Nimboya sent help to Zengu at Hammerfall, who oversaw its recovery for future fighting against Zul'Gurub's trolls.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to speak with Zengu at Hammerfall.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Zengu at Hammerfall in Arathi Highlands.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="227243660435d4708d68bdcca9e784ac655c552e48e684ea539b0c60cd00f021",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[639]={["aftermath"]="Zengu accepted the first step toward removing the sword from Trollbane's tomb.",["atomIDs"]={"639:description:1-133","639:description:135-213","639:description:218-294","639:description:299-418","639:description:423-506","639:objective:1-47"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"639:completion:1-15","639:completion:17-115"},["opening"]="Zengu recalled the sword once borne against his people by Ignaeus of Strom. The ruined kingdom's survivors had divided its protecting sigils, and the Syndicate held the first sought from Stromgarde.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover the Syndicate-held sigil.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the sigil to Zengu.",["sourceHash"]="24bcf6f293f2c9d7f3fca5f6c484058058e05df52f13e0d0cc4158f64836602e",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[640]={["aftermath"]="Tor'gan found all pieces present and prepared to reform their magical structure.",["atomIDs"]={"640:description:1-106","640:description:108-204","640:description:209-327","640:description:329-446","640:objective:1-105"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"640:completion:1-42","640:completion:44-75","640:completion:77-156","640:completion:161-194"},["opening"]="One sigil was secured, but the militia held the rest. Galen had divided Thoradin's into five pieces; Tor'gan's magic could reconstruct it if all were recovered.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring the five fragments to Tor'gan.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the fragments in Hammerfall.",["sourceHash"]="60831f2aaec3fa4177bfbb202376e5c19d046c01704742742dcb1c47ea39fcea",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[641]={["aftermath"]="Zengu still lacked certainty about the next sigil's location because its holders traveled through Arathi.",["atomIDs"]={"641:description:1-37","641:description:39-103","641:description:105-177","641:objective:1-60"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"641:completion:1-71","641:completion:73-225"},["opening"]="Tor'gan's reconstruction had succeeded. The restored sigil could now serve the tomb's lock and belonged with Zengu's growing collection.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to return the restored sigil.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Thoradin's sigil to Zengu.",["sourceHash"]="f79d279f0dd8e359fe167170eaba3f8a36843efb20b4b53028fb14d1001299dd",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[642]={["aftermath"]="Myzrael reported feeling more herself, while saying she remained far from freedom.",["atomIDs"]={"642:description:1-19","642:description:22-129","642:description:132-204","642:description:209-223","642:description:226-337","642:description:340-432","642:description:437-458","642:objective:1-89"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"642:completion:5-31","642:completion:33-59","642:completion:64-100"},["opening"]="Myzrael spoke through crystals as her only link to the surface. She blamed giants for her confinement and their kobold allies for guarding another cluster that could be powered with collected motes.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather twelve motes for the eastern shards.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} activated the Drywhisker cluster with the motes.",["sourceHash"]="3d21ef3f48d1bb6d96990bdedc8c1ef749ce27d149ba800f9461221e3fb7cb83",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[643]={["aftermath"]="Zengu counted one final sigil still needed before the sword could be taken.",["atomIDs"]={"643:description:1-167","643:description:169-252","643:description:257-375","643:description:377-418","643:objective:1-67"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"643:completion:1-80","643:completion:82-178"},["opening"]="Zengu could not explain the prince's roaming cavalry, but knew its leader held another sigil. Finding Valorcall would turn the moving patrol into the next source of access to the tomb.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover Valorcall's sigil.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the cavalry's sigil to Zengu.",["sourceHash"]="8f6cc00e6072bc4e63befb4b728d54bd2e53de4c0031ce0c74b29747767f1497",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[644]={["aftermath"]="Zengu regarded the collection as complete and anticipated turning the sword against Zul'Gurub's trolls.",["atomIDs"]={"644:description:1-100","644:description:102-178","644:description:180-286","644:objective:1-84"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"644:completion:1-24","644:completion:26-143","644:completion:145-214"},["opening"]="Galen personally held the final sigil in Stromgarde's militia chapel. Zengu warned that the prince was both heavily protected and a capable warrior.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover Galen's sigil.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the final sigil to Zengu.",["sourceHash"]="c498f8ee0d0d6bdb632781d114fcd856debcc74fc9d62892987bc8d2c742a318",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[645]={["aftermath"]="The sigil was consumed in a flash, releasing the sword from the stone hands that held it.",["atomIDs"]={"645:description:1-12","645:description:14-98","645:description:100-195","645:description:200-279","645:description:281-300","645:objective:1-56"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"645:completion:1-210"},["opening"]="The assembled sigils joined into one. Zengu took that union as the means to break the tomb's wards in the sanctum behind Stromgarde's chapel.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to open the tomb and recover its sword.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} unlocked the resting place.",["sourceHash"]="c65cf0e6fda3049fb29c19968ce6e1ae130611453883c36e87ba83b421ec4a78",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[646]={["aftermath"]="Zengu promised to send it onward to Nimboya and hoped it would transform the struggle in Zul'Gurub.",["atomIDs"]={"646:description:1-91","646:objective:1-42"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"646:completion:1-68","646:completion:70-111","646:completion:113-184","646:completion:189-269","646:completion:274-339"},["opening"]="The fading light left the sword released from its stone sheath. Its next destination was Hammerfall, where Zengu awaited the weapon his people had once feared.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to deliver the released sword.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Trol'kalar to Zengu.",["sourceHash"]="c4e100ddf6e644e6ffc1a7a69274fd8e63771ad3e86e1f4b13095f29986bb7c9",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[647]={["atomIDs"]={"647:description:1-48","647:description:51-124","647:description:129-162","647:description:165-247","647:description:252-275","647:description:277-376","647:description:381-434","647:description:437-474","647:description:477-486","647:objective:1-62"},["opening"]="Foggy MacKreel had only fifteen minutes left to settle a debt with Brewmeister Bilger. After a night of too much Moonshine, he entrusted a fresh batch to a quicker traveler bound for Southshore.",["pending"]="{actor} would hurry MacKreel's Moonshine to Brewmeister Bilger.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered MacKreel's Moonshine to Bilger in Southshore.",["sourceHash"]="988a4090c5324d1591e042258c4cd494ffbe7373187050abc90d7989cb28edd0",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[648]={["atomIDs"]={"648:description:1-53","648:description:58-151","648:description:154-234","648:description:237-326","648:description:329-400","648:description:405-473","648:description:476-503","648:objective:1-88"},["bridge"]="The beacon had reached the crashed robot. Oglethorpe now needed OOX-17/TN escorted to Steamwheedle Port while he restored its systems for takeoff.",["bridgeFrom"]=351,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Oglethorpe needed OOX-17/TN brought to open ground while its cloaking system was restored. Steamwheedle Port provided the destination for a lengthy takeoff, with a report due afterward in Booty Bay.",["pending"]="{actor} would escort OOX-17/TN to Steamwheedle Port and report to Oglethorpe.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed OOX-17/TN's escort to Steamwheedle Port and reported to Oglethorpe.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="1c1c7b37a7cf4f93fab9e11f814625cd48732e2a6614e290179b3b72027200e3",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[649]={["aftermath"]="Malton explained that packaging would raise the tavern sale's price and named an independent high-elf drinking companion who could supply it.",["atomIDs"]={"649:description:1-117","649:description:120-126","649:description:131-154","649:description:159-257","649:description:260-303","649:description:306-447","649:description:450-498","649:objective:1-37"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"649:completion:1-36","649:completion:38-156","649:completion:158-237","649:completion:239-263","649:completion:268-330","649:completion:332-398","649:completion:400-436"},["opening"]="Dran's salvage interest lay in a drink no longer commonly obtained. An abandoned outpost held the desired stock, and Malton knew a contact who could recover its valuable original presentation.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to ask Malton for the details.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} consulted Dran's son.",["sourceHash"]="42412ea23d0cc9cfd0ae98057fa7e8feb842ed33d51d78b153eafea4fb7919ce",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[650]={["aftermath"]="Gilveradin recognized Malton and praised drink as something crossing treaties and alliances.",["atomIDs"]={"650:description:1-57","650:description:60-118","650:description:121-190","650:description:193-271","650:description:273-304","650:description:307-380","650:description:385-484","650:description:487-495","650:objective:1-69"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"650:completion:1-23","650:completion:25-64","650:completion:66-175","650:completion:177-287","650:completion:292-394"},["opening"]="Malton named Gilveradin as both wine expert and packer. The requested stock had to cover a case for sale, bottles for Dran and whatever fee the contact demanded.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to find Gilveradin in the Hinterlands.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached the drinking companion.",["sourceHash"]="2877ed3a8a3c38a7ee40e3333db98a51edb0e8e3985fb5e7fc1b188852e46ec6",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[651]={["aftermath"]="Myzrael said her shackles had loosened and freedom was drawing closer.",["atomIDs"]={"651:description:1-55","651:description:58-103","651:description:108-180","651:description:183-240","651:description:245-349","651:objective:1-153","651:objective:158-198"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"651:completion:1-35","651:completion:40-56","651:completion:58-90","651:completion:92-162","651:completion:167-189","651:completion:191-201"},["opening"]="Myzrael described four binding stones, with the strongest locked by keys from the other three. Guardians watched the separate sites, making the proposed release a journey across Arathi.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather the three keys for the inner stone.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} opened the bindings with the collected keys.",["sourceHash"]="a34a5fe5d445a6d67d681c8b2b89445937774da9d7b2fbc53ed7a3f75f4ec639",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[652]={["aftermath"]="A shudder passed beneath the stone when the rod was fitted into it.",["atomIDs"]={"652:description:1-97","652:description:100-154","652:description:157-223","652:description:228-345","652:description:350-385","652:description:388-470","652:objective:1-21","652:objective:24-86"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"652:completion:1-34","652:completion:36-71"},["opening"]="The loosened bindings still left a keystone lock. Myzrael identified Fozruk as the keeper of its rod and pressed for one more act to complete her release.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover the rod and bring it to the keystone.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} placed the recovered rod in the keystone.",["sourceHash"]="bca383530c8119935ab7ad5a0c3a76fb29e748326f7060537bf67afdef124c48",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[653]={["aftermath"]="Gerrig had been told to expect the visitor and welcomed another servant of what he called a higher cause.",["atomIDs"]={"653:description:1-17","653:description:22-26","653:description:29-38","653:description:41-93","653:description:96-170","653:description:175-256","653:description:261-285","653:description:288-323","653:description:326-386","653:description:391-417","653:description:420-471","653:description:474-504","653:objective:1-62"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"653:completion:1-36","653:completion:38-103"},["opening"]="Myzrael announced freedom but intended to gather strength in hiding before confronting her captors. She directed a future summoning through Gerrig in Ironforge.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to consult Gerrig about summoning her.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Gerrig in the Forlorn Cavern.",["sourceHash"]="e40e71b98515c10f11a9328a3a199ed58ca75077cb530b38e05854db1a408e2b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[654]={["aftermath"]="Bilgewhizzle removed the power source so the collected data could be kept without the earlier expiry risk.",["atomIDs"]={"654:description:1-82","654:description:85-123","654:description:128-243","654:description:246-369","654:description:374-420","654:objective:1-70","654:objective:73-176"},["bridge"]="The power source was available, starting the testing kit's two-hour limit. Eight acceptable samples of each required desert creature had to return before the data were lost.",["bridgeFrom"]=379,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"654:completion:1-73","654:completion:75-180"},["opening"]="The activated kit glowed and vibrated, starting a two-hour window for the field data. Eight acceptable samples from each desert creature type had to be returned before the power and information were lost.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to obtain eight acceptable basilisk, hyena and scorpid samples within the limit.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the testing kit with eight acceptable samples of each required creature type before the power source expired.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="12c139f0345f69add7419ef75269c52276152f2e0b288f5fa501fc71822d8ce4",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[655]={["aftermath"]="Tor'gan explained that Gor'mul had been left behind during the liberation and wandered for years before the Horde returned.",["atomIDs"]={"655:description:1-42","655:description:44-125","655:description:127-148","655:description:150-172","655:description:174-231","655:description:236-244","655:description:246-260","655:description:262-323","655:description:325-398","655:description:400-418","655:description:420-439","655:description:441-461","655:objective:1-33"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"655:completion:1-25","655:completion:27-111","655:completion:116-258","655:completion:260-383"},["opening"]="Gor'mul's recollection of captivity ended with Doomhammer struck from behind. The memory left him questioning hope, and the inquiry turned toward Tor'gan in Hammerfall.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to speak with Tor'gan about Gor'mul.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Gor'mul's condition to the shaman.",["sourceHash"]="21b0adeffa1a0dc36b715971724ff8f18a7e258b5ec0832c7438d237c169af83",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[656]={["aftermath"]="A wail and roar rose from below. The crystals pulsed with menace toward the surface.",["atomIDs"]={"656:description:1-53","656:description:56-141","656:description:144-273","656:description:278-293","656:description:298-379","656:description:382-466","656:description:471-509","656:objective:1-55","656:objective:60-127"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"656:completion:1-95","656:completion:97-129","656:completion:134-221","656:completion:223-259","656:completion:261-323"},["opening"]="Theldurin warned that Myzrael would challenge her captors once strong enough. His answer was to summon and defeat her at the first shards, then restore the binding with her shackles.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to summon Myzrael and bind her again.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned her shackles to the shards.",["sourceHash"]="290547ae18787557dd755acc67de4e0d88475744256d71b2e3f3a35e7fff8fbe",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[662]={["aftermath"]="The secured information was ready for the command in Booty Bay.",["atomIDs"]={"662:description:1-36","662:description:39-96","662:description:99-213","662:description:216-246","662:description:251-295","662:description:297-328","662:description:331-372","662:description:377-447","662:description:450-504","662:objective:1-114"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"662:completion:1-84","662:completion:86-99"},["opening"]="Two ships sank when an unnatural falling tide drove them onto a temple-like reef. Nilzlix needed their logs and charts retrieved before the surviving crew could leave sensitive information behind.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to salvage both ships' records.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the charts and logs to Nilzlix.",["sourceHash"]="996ea66f3994b1f1e032660223e678e68262bf987f2988e3e68ed09c2c9c766f",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[663]={["aftermath"]="O'Breen described a rumbling sea and a sudden fall in the tide, then asked for help for the crew.",["atomIDs"]={"663:description:1-20","663:description:22-52","663:description:57-81","663:description:84-138","663:description:141-206","663:description:211-272","663:description:275-321","663:description:324-368","663:description:371-409","663:description:414-491","663:objective:1-41"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"663:completion:1-12","663:completion:17-38","663:completion:40-96","663:completion:101-183","663:completion:185-295","663:completion:300-320","663:completion:322-379","663:completion:384-404","663:completion:406-431","663:completion:436-486"},["opening"]="Lolo welcomed a traveler to a voyage delayed by catastrophe. Two ships lay below the cove, and the surviving captain was the person to consult before joining the stranded expedition.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to speak with O'Breen.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met the captain in the cove.",["sourceHash"]="df801e49d3944cb4730fad89d858936ce8d950271aa8a8bcdc1a1a39b682fdd0",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[664]={["aftermath"]="Steelgut found some solace in the news while acknowledging that it could not restore those lost.",["atomIDs"]={"664:description:1-27","664:description:29-119","664:description:124-182","664:description:184-218","664:description:223-278","664:description:280-313","664:description:318-374","664:description:376-392","664:description:394-418","664:description:420-438","664:description:440-477","664:description:482-506","664:objective:1-105"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"664:completion:1-24","664:completion:29-62","664:completion:64-163"},["opening"]="Steelgut survived the sinking but lost his ship and crew. He blamed naga for killing the other survivors and sought retaliation from the shore where he had been rescued.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to confront the raiders and sorceresses.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Steelgut's naga assignment.",["sourceHash"]="0df4a45a271d0a31f3f126ad96cef30eca1b949c6fa99bcd7d7f7bab82b54a75",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[665]={["aftermath"]="Draxlegauge confirmed that the charged goggles worked.",["atomIDs"]={"665:description:1-73","665:description:75-113","665:description:118-187","665:description:189-243","665:description:245-351","665:description:356-378","665:description:380-414","665:description:416-486","665:objective:1-52"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"665:completion:1-31","665:completion:33-46"},["opening"]="The gems were nearly impossible to locate in dark water without the doctor's goggles. Charging them required an enchanted cave stone, and Phizzlethorpe needed protection from the ambushes there.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to guard the professor's trip to the stone.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the cave escort.",["sourceHash"]="443ed2b82c08de063a7bb51df9e73789982ab3cc1738949ece97334d03c4e14a",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[666]={["atomIDs"]={"666:description:1-93","666:description:95-172","666:description:177-219","666:description:224-338","666:description:343-471","666:objective:1-127"},["opening"]="Calcification had concealed the seabed gems within thick stone. The charged goggles offered a way to distinguish the lost treasure, with the borrowed equipment due back after the search.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover ten gems and return the goggles.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the gems and returned the equipment.",["sourceHash"]="0fc3bdcda1ef3fea1812edfb27fe40f400446fb8a59cc8953b8ce0992db42c90",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[667]={["aftermath"]="O'Breen confirmed the crew survived and planned to depart when the tide rose.",["atomIDs"]={"667:description:1-12","667:description:14-66","667:description:71-118","667:description:120-160","667:description:165-252","667:description:254-341","667:description:346-382","667:description:384-443","667:description:445-479","667:description:484-501","667:objective:1-41"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"667:completion:1-23","667:completion:28-69","667:completion:74-120","667:completion:122-191","667:completion:193-235","667:completion:240-268"},["opening"]="The Daggerspines were gathering for an attack on the captain. O'Breen needed help with the cannon and shoreline defense because the surviving crew still depended on his navigation to get home.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to protect O'Breen during the attack.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the captain's defense.",["sourceHash"]="86bc9fc4dee93b4f6c8e478fa674beb9e22518e32590a6fc0a82ecdfac308426",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[668]={["atomIDs"]={"668:description:1-40","668:description:42-81","668:description:83-115","668:description:120-296","668:description:301-332","668:objective:1-39"},["opening"]="The recovered gems had to reach O'Breen before the scholars lingered too long with pirate treasure. Draxlegauge passed them onward, wary of how possession might be interpreted.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to bring the gems to the captain.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the recovered treasure to O'Breen.",["sourceHash"]="87af4a88c884b0cd4452d80bc2892089cd39eb869fa78be56f9564f2124534e6",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[669]={["aftermath"]="Seahorn welcomed the discovery and credited his choice of captain.",["atomIDs"]={"669:description:1-62","669:description:67-137","669:description:139-249","669:description:254-431","669:description:434-463","669:objective:1-63"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"669:completion:1-40","669:completion:42-94"},["opening"]="O'Breen could not leave with the tide low and naga watching. He sent a sample to Booty Bay as proof of the discovery and news that further extraction was underway.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to carry the sample to Seahorn.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the gem and news.",["sourceHash"]="f5a43db66e9ae53cad952ab69be156df08a32c6066229cd2e1e1ac283750536d",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[670]={["atomIDs"]={"670:description:1-44","670:description:46-97","670:description:102-256","670:description:261-325","670:objective:1-63"},["opening"]="Seahorn's own fleet was delayed by restocking. Secret correspondence still needed to reach O'Breen off Arathi, linking the cove's stranded crew to business beyond its immediate trouble.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to carry the confidential letter.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Seahorn's message to O'Breen.",["sourceHash"]="9a2afda943ecf06dcf65533dc1a08f30bc9cdba58dc99ab89c9d6f5293ce515e",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[671]={["aftermath"]="Tor'gan remained troubled by demonic associations and needed time to determine the Syndicate's intentions.",["atomIDs"]={"671:description:1-39","671:description:41-75","671:description:77-96","671:description:98-228","671:description:230-296","671:description:301-383","671:description:385-422","671:description:424-488","671:description:490-511","671:objective:1-52"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"671:completion:1-148","671:completion:150-182"},["opening"]="Tor'gan's unease had led him to traces of summoning at Northfold. A depleted bloodstone amulet suggested the means, but he dared not return for active samples himself.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather ten bloodstone amulets.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Tor'gan with the amulets.",["sourceHash"]="6baf280e8cc9d95d5bd2c4e212119c61bc01d9424e899609a1925afa16460e71",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[672]={["aftermath"]="Tor'gan planned an amulet whose strength would come from the raptors' spirits.",["atomIDs"]={"672:description:1-133","672:description:138-217","672:description:219-233","672:description:235-242","672:description:244-320","672:description:322-339","672:description:344-387","672:description:389-444","672:objective:1-104"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"672:completion:1-10","672:completion:12-107"},["opening"]="Stories of Orgrimmar and Thrall had failed to comfort Gor'mul. Tor'gan proposed a small enchanted object as a demonstration of the Horde's new shamanistic power.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather ten raptor eyes.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the eyes to Tor'gan.",["sourceHash"]="a016075743568389b8205f28fe1bbad19db338c33e6eea32a360adea11d7e031",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[673]={["aftermath"]="The shaman regarded it as a reminder of the orcs' former bondage and looked forward to destroying it.",["atomIDs"]={"673:description:1-92","673:description:94-208","673:description:210-249","673:description:254-283","673:description:285-442","673:objective:1-75"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"673:completion:1-80","673:completion:82-95","673:completion:97-223"},["opening"]="Tor'gan now believed a powerful warlock in Stromgarde was using a relic to summon many demons. He sought the object so its power could be destroyed rather than merely left without a bearer.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover Marez's orb.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the bloodstone orb to Tor'gan.",["sourceHash"]="4db98b8b63bd6a0ab3084757278f73dc11a004ee11745402dce7908e55b9b4c0",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[674]={["aftermath"]="Gor'mul dismissed it as polished bone and questioned whether a trinket could restore the Horde's glory.",["atomIDs"]={"674:description:1-139","674:objective:1-40"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"674:completion:1-13","674:completion:15-28","674:completion:30-63","674:completion:65-110"},["opening"]="The amulet was prepared as a possible answer to Gor'mul's despair. Tor'gan hoped raptor strength would awaken the warrior he remembered.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to bring the amulet to Gor'mul.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} gave Gor'mul the raptor amulet.",["sourceHash"]="743431e9575c0242419c11b9ed18cec6934e59733194d7c0870549e245784442",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[675]={["aftermath"]="Tor'gan admitted the failure but still believed a greater display of shamanic power might reach him.",["atomIDs"]={"675:description:1-44","675:description:49-76","675:description:78-81","675:description:83-140","675:description:142-218","675:description:220-252","675:objective:1-19"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"675:completion:1-23","675:completion:25-140","675:completion:142-212"},["opening"]="Gor'mul threw the amulet aside. He rejected Tor'gan's mercy while dwelling on his inability to die beside Doomhammer.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to tell Tor'gan how the attempt ended.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned to Tor'gan with Gor'mul's response.",["sourceHash"]="586058fbe5f55de67cb151fa649cc8316542abd29ac13214592bd2a8c069877c",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[676]={["atomIDs"]={"676:description:1-12","676:description:14-25","676:description:27-59","676:description:61-96","676:description:98-114","676:description:119-166","676:description:168-223","676:description:228-297","676:description:299-384","676:description:386-474","676:objective:1-120"},["opening"]="Hammerfall needed reinforcements, but Tallow first demanded a test against Boulderfist ogres. Only afterward did he direct recruits to Drum Fel.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to face the ogres and report at Hammerfall.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Tallow's test and reached Drum Fel.",["sourceHash"]="3be3498770431850f8ab95ae8fa4ac33c32dc88d3f5f72cf43b732d2bdf85eae",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[677]={["atomIDs"]={"677:description:1-166","677:description:168-230","677:description:236-365","677:description:370-435","677:description:437-511","677:objective:1-118"},["opening"]="Drum Fel saw Witherbark and Boulderfist cooperation as a threat to Hammerfall's place in Arathi. His first attack focused on the trolls' southern camps.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to confront the three Witherbark groups.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Drum Fel's first campaign assignment.",["sourceHash"]="739e65f38a8eb18de6b10d23d9964e8864155da64328745ede4db734049a600a",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[678]={["atomIDs"]={"678:description:1-29","678:description:31-75","678:description:80-289","678:description:294-403","678:description:405-462","678:objective:1-100"},["opening"]="The next trial turned from trolls to the ogres southwest of Hammerfall. Drum Fel regarded their brutes and magi as a greater challenge to the outpost's defenders.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to confront the Boulderfist brutes and magi.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the ogre-lair assignment.",["sourceHash"]="3d69cb8fa391c0967b2e0b0b72647e5961aed647f7b7659eafb967e811df6356",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[679]={["aftermath"]="Drum Fel considered the threat greatly reduced and hoped the outpost could begin to thrive.",["atomIDs"]={"679:description:1-49","679:description:51-71","679:description:73-155","679:description:157-272","679:description:277-382","679:objective:1-99"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"679:completion:1-29","679:completion:31-128"},["opening"]="Drum Fel judged the campaign ready for a strike at its leadership. Boulderfist lords and their shamans occupied Stromgarde's ruins and directed attacks on Hammerfall.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to confront the leaders in Stromgarde.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Drum Fel's final leadership assignment.",["sourceHash"]="974fcddfa5e2b7d5f6511726cf52f26bc7a2729f32ca6a0962e570f192642451",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[680]={["aftermath"]="Korin credited the act with protecting her husband and the outpost for another day.",["atomIDs"]={"680:description:1-83","680:description:88-242","680:description:247-367","680:description:372-499","680:objective:1-72"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"680:completion:1-37","680:completion:39-152","680:completion:154-199"},["opening"]="Korin concealed Or'Kalar's presence from her husband, fearing Drum Fel would rush into revenge. Her auguries suggested a trap born of an old defeat, and she sought another hand against it.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring Or'Kalar's head to Korin.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the head at Hammerfall.",["sourceHash"]="3cf4cf4497e59b2cb94b37b3c241492c1ec4e0b2f2dba54a8425fbce59a1a254",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[681]={["aftermath"]="Nials hoped fewer enemies there would allow more supplies through and preserve the cause.",["atomIDs"]={"681:description:1-56","681:description:59-183","681:description:188-232","681:description:237-363","681:description:368-425","681:description:428-510","681:objective:1-57","681:objective:62-102"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"681:completion:1-14","681:completion:16-123","681:completion:128-158"},["opening"]="Nials described a losing war inside a city divided among militia, ogres and Syndicate. The manor's control of intervening ground made even supplies from Southshore difficult to receive.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to strike the Syndicate at Northfold.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Nials's manor assignment.",["sourceHash"]="4388382be54d139a78a57d94dbb39d4bcae735669bb4f0b24e35748bd7e475da",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[682]={["aftermath"]="The militia planned to notify the soldiers' families, replacing uncertainty with grim news of their deaths.",["atomIDs"]={"682:description:1-75","682:description:77-273","682:description:278-380","682:description:385-463","682:objective:1-60"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"682:completion:1-14","682:completion:16-100","682:completion:105-195"},["opening"]="The Syndicate paid bounties for badges stripped from fallen militiamen. Nials wanted those trophies reclaimed from the city's occupied quarter.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover seven Stromgarde badges.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the badges to Nials.",["sourceHash"]="21866aeb2973c23e7acbe490703ca9e97fe90b5a20db727c538b01f563193120",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[683]={["atomIDs"]={"683:description:1-45","683:description:50-138","683:description:140-261","683:description:266-359","683:description:362-383","683:objective:1-63"},["opening"]="Grief kept Sara from presenting her own plea at Ironforge's court. She prepared a note for Magni and entrusted the short but painful public errand to another.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to take Sara Balloo's note to Magni.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Sara Balloo's note to King Magni Bronzebeard.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="a99f1146ef2abf8b289325ffb1ec9a4969fd266c808b376b67e5683ae2b54fe5",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[684]={["aftermath"]="Nials welcomed her removal while treating a connection to a darker power as rumor.",["atomIDs"]={"684:description:1-104","684:description:107-180","684:description:185-227","684:description:232-320","684:description:323-366","684:objective:1-53"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"684:completion:1-25","684:completion:27-40","684:completion:42-58","684:completion:63-191","684:completion:193-251"},["opening"]="The militia's notice identified Marez as a senior Syndicate operative and cunning warlock. Her last known position lay inside the organization's Stromgarde territory.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to pursue Marez's bounty.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Marez's head to Nials.",["sourceHash"]="0f13e19f89f7d0863f6a3b5e69efdbec2784164f4c8bbe0473f6a30208bab7c1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[685]={["atomIDs"]={"685:description:1-100","685:description:103-231","685:description:236-348","685:description:353-403","685:objective:1-75"},["opening"]="Falconcrest directed the Syndicate's Arathi efforts, while Otto protected him and had killed many defenders. The paired bounty joined a strategic leader to a dangerous bodyguard.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover both heads for Nials.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the heads of Falconcrest and Otto.",["sourceHash"]="dcfcec2e568c6fb177a2219c67ed183fac2719d6c2851a9b4ad9609e93488256",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[686]={["atomIDs"]={"686:description:1-38","686:description:40-137","686:description:139-256","686:description:261-349","686:description:354-443","686:description:448-472","686:description:474-510","686:objective:1-70"},["bridge"]="Sara's plea had reached the king. Magni could not restore her husband, but ordered a memorial and sent the commission to Marblesten.",["bridgeFrom"]=683,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Magni could not restore Sully to Sara, but he could order remembrance. A commission for Grand Mason Marblesten would make the fallen soldier's loss visible in a lasting memorial.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to convey Magni's commission to Marblesten.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Grand Mason Marblesten about the king's memorial.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="649ec407f53157887d3dc2e45cf012e4a90d4a27967dfe3437c3e89ac1543d57",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[687]={["atomIDs"]={"687:description:1-73","687:description:76-122","687:description:125-183","687:description:186-268","687:description:273-327","687:description:330-369","687:objective:1-24"},["opening"]="Gerrig named his order as Twilight's Hammer and accused Theldurin of stealing Myzrael's scroll before fleeing. Rumor placed the former member in the Badlands.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to locate Theldurin and the stolen scroll.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} found Theldurin.",["sourceHash"]="cf62c1d5b7b992220a863525e4a70b8e4e1ae808bd54b74b074d10e8e0db9c4b",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[688]={["aftermath"]="Zaruk said Myzrael had announced the visitor and prepared to discuss bringing her to the surface.",["atomIDs"]={"688:description:1-17","688:description:22-26","688:description:29-38","688:description:41-93","688:description:96-170","688:description:175-256","688:description:261-285","688:description:288-323","688:description:326-385","688:description:390-420","688:description:423-453","688:objective:1-31"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"688:completion:1-12","688:completion:14-132"},["opening"]="Myzrael planned to hide and gather strength before facing her captors. This route to her later summoning led through Zaruk in Hammerfall rather than directly back to the shards.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to consult Zaruk about the summoning.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met Zaruk in Hammerfall.",["sourceHash"]="ccacd476e23076ed5e519fe811bb10ba899b07a17081214bed89684f6ca993b1",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[689]={["atomIDs"]={"689:description:1-86","689:description:89-151","689:description:156-196","689:description:201-266","689:description:268-362","689:description:364-437","689:objective:1-70"},["bridge"]="The royal commission had reached Marblesten. Alterac Granite from Darrow Hill was his chosen material for Sully Balloo's lasting tribute.",["bridgeFrom"]=686,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Marblesten sought stone worthy of the royal memorial. Five pieces of Alterac Granite from Darrow Hill would give Sully Balloo's tribute the enduring material he wanted.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather five pieces of Alterac Granite for Marblesten.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered five pieces of Alterac Granite to Grand Mason Marblesten.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="ce883697c253c8a06d5767ebba77672dabe8855c2748a06b37cc7a8bedf7428d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[690]={["atomIDs"]={"690:description:1-14","690:description:16-106","690:description:111-283","690:description:288-379","690:description:381-458","690:description:460-478","690:objective:1-54"},["opening"]="Trelane's attempt to defend Stromgarde had failed, leaving possessions behind in the besieged city. Malin's agents at Refuge Pointe needed more help with the recovery.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to meet Skuerto at Refuge Pointe.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Skuerto in the Arathi Highlands.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="8d876e04c5520008776457a3899eea30e1356e502d7cf10a6ea5300c459bf02d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[691]={["aftermath"]="Kryten directed further conversation toward Skuerto, who had returned from scouting the ogres.",["atomIDs"]={"691:description:1-67","691:description:69-182","691:description:187-280","691:description:285-312","691:description:314-360","691:objective:1-121"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"691:completion:1-11","691:completion:13-82","691:completion:87-165","691:completion:170-274","691:completion:279-350","691:completion:352-449"},["opening"]="Kryten and Skuerto were gathering reagents for Malin. The apprentice needed tusks, medicine pouches and a knife from Arathi's southeastern Witherbark camps.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather Kryten's three kinds of reagents.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the requested objects to Kryten.",["sourceHash"]="dac7d02c82e662b285310a4d0beb15612ed6f57376a85201f48c38a2e9d533df",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[692]={["aftermath"]="Theldurin began looking for a way to join the pieces, with their protective value still a hope.",["atomIDs"]={"692:description:1-47","692:description:50-69","692:description:72-157","692:description:162-186","692:description:189-214","692:description:217-286","692:description:289-323","692:description:328-353","692:description:356-431","692:description:436-496","692:objective:1-114"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"692:completion:1-19","692:completion:21-34","692:completion:36-102","692:completion:107-185"},["opening"]="Theldurin feared the scroll could summon Myzrael, yet thought it might also be needed against her. Elementals had torn it apart and contested the pieces.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover all three scroll fragments.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the fragments to Theldurin.",["sourceHash"]="d3b3101d8a7a4fa2486ddf1e85a317eba9965c698990292786c532ba2f09b705",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[693]={["aftermath"]="One object was recovered; Skuerto identified three more in Stromgarde and urged rest before the harder phase.",["atomIDs"]={"693:description:1-8","693:description:10-48","693:description:50-74","693:description:79-166","693:description:168-312","693:description:317-379","693:description:381-417","693:description:422-493","693:objective:1-76"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"693:completion:1-14","693:completion:16-68","693:completion:70-113","693:completion:118-224","693:completion:226-287"},["opening"]="Skuerto traced the first of Trelane's missing objects to Kor'gresh. The ogre was already using its ice magic against his own kin in Boulderfist Hall.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover Trelane's wand.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the wand to Skuerto.",["sourceHash"]="06c7cff386f5fe382153a0b2aa81c55f267ab6289a149249f542963c0db66957",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[694]={["aftermath"]="Kryten prepared the spell needed to turn the agate into a working key.",["atomIDs"]={"694:description:1-11","694:description:16-98","694:description:100-229","694:description:231-315","694:description:317-402","694:description:407-511","694:objective:1-71"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"694:completion:1-17","694:completion:19-34","694:completion:39-120"},["opening"]="Ogres surrounded the tower holding the remaining objects. An agate stolen from it could be enchanted into a key, allowing its defenses to support the recovery.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring an azure agate to Kryten.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Kryten with the gem.",["sourceHash"]="f22f4e0464f2195f2112130b5a7369287d3bf3f9449e13544f835e2db2f4f20d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[695]={["atomIDs"]={"695:description:1-17","695:description:19-132","695:description:134-212","695:description:218-234","695:description:236-281","695:description:283-324","695:description:326-376","695:objective:1-17"},["opening"]="Kryten's enchanted gem could activate the tower at a pedestal near its base. Skuerto still held the details of what should be recovered from inside.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to hear Skuerto's remaining instructions.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Skuerto after the enchantment.",["sourceHash"]="e36e2db72ff0fc77b9b9e6e331934a7dc516e35e104049f13bb663545c281993",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[696]={["aftermath"]="Skuerto considered the mission an overwhelming success and expected Malin to be pleased.",["atomIDs"]={"696:description:1-93","696:description:98-250","696:description:255-358","696:description:360-459","696:description:464-489","696:objective:1-113"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"696:completion:1-70","696:completion:72-95","696:completion:100-171"},["opening"]="Skuerto named a phylactery, orb and ember agate in the tower's chests. Its defenses would help but not remove the danger from the ogres around them.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover Trelane's three remaining objects.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered all three to Skuerto.",["sourceHash"]="66040283e0e8c94f9fcee98f994af9342f805897bc95a682e156febe579737c4",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[697]={["aftermath"]="Malin welcomed the success, Trelane's recovered property and the prospect of his researchers coming home.",["atomIDs"]={"697:description:1-88","697:description:90-158","697:description:163-176","697:objective:1-74"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"697:completion:1-58","697:completion:63-91","697:completion:93-106","697:completion:108-134","697:completion:136-235","697:completion:240-253","697:completion:255-301"},["opening"]="Skuerto's sealed letter carried news that the two researchers would soon return. The successful recovery was ready to be reported to their patron in Stormwind.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to take the letter to Malin.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Skuerto's report.",["sourceHash"]="dc9f3abcf71c6ff46798555166eef90af43a4e4bb435679588acf3fed5ed4570",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[698]={["atomIDs"]={"698:description:1-216","698:description:221-331","698:description:333-364","698:description:369-491","698:objective:1-66"},["opening"]="Dar's supplies had fallen behind the beach outpost's needs. Tok'Kar divided his time between guarding and cooking, and the soldiers preferred meat from mature sawtooths.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to bring eight sawtooth flanks to the outpost.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Tok'Kar with the meat.",["sourceHash"]="a049c4ce1e13264c0c90db3df491fa353c5a5c2e0184eb0f9e8d9767c84ccccf",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[699]={["aftermath"]="Tok'Kar accepted the materials and prepared to craft another weapon.",["atomIDs"]={"699:description:1-149","699:description:151-242","699:description:247-320","699:description:322-453","699:objective:1-66"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"699:completion:1-38","699:completion:43-76","699:completion:78-163","699:completion:168-219","699:completion:221-251","699:completion:253-306"},["opening"]="The coastal watch left Tok'Kar little leisure. Prepared snapper claws would add weapons for the soldiers protecting Stonard from the murloc threat.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather six snapper claws.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the claws to Tok'Kar.",["sourceHash"]="6fd78bb5ed0180820376f4853051b25b01a2d1d18d2dbf51a206374ff8fb906f",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[700]={["aftermath"]="Magni regarded the memorial as small beside the value of a life. He hoped it would remind future generations why soldiers like Sully had died.",["atomIDs"]={"700:description:1-41","700:description:44-85","700:description:90-126","700:description:128-180","700:description:185-276","700:objective:1-33"},["bridge"]="The granite had reached the mason and the memorial was finished. Word of the completed royal commission was ready to return to Magni.",["bridgeFrom"]=689,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"700:completion:1-69","700:completion:71-122","700:completion:127-237","700:completion:239-343"},["opening"]="The granite had become a completed memorial. Marblesten wanted the king told that his commission for Sully Balloo had been carried out.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to report completion of the memorial to Magni.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported to King Magni Bronzebeard.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="3c9b86eb20397b2ed193c4a0bdbbe3b87db77095038fcc9eca42f9b0f29f58d6",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[701]={["aftermath"]="Tor'gan prepared an orb intended to carry both raptor strength and intelligence.",["atomIDs"]={"701:description:1-116","701:description:118-244","701:description:249-307","701:objective:1-65"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"701:completion:1-31","701:completion:33-104","701:completion:106-188"},["opening"]="Tor'gan had not abandoned the attempt to reach Gor'mul. Hearts from the fleshstalkers would support a stronger raptor enchantment than the discarded amulet.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather twelve raptor hearts.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the hearts to Tor'gan.",["sourceHash"]="51b93bf342c0285922dfb8cd1ec63ef75b78108293f9fb1aa38dbcc9bd494960",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[702]={["aftermath"]="Gor'mul found its power interesting, a different response from his earlier rejection.",["atomIDs"]={"702:description:1-75","702:description:77-148","702:description:150-303","702:objective:1-30"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"702:completion:1-63","702:completion:65-91"},["opening"]="The new orb was ready, and Tor'gan hoped it would give Gor'mul a reason to listen. An explanation of the changed Horde was meant to follow that first opening.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to take the orb to Gor'mul.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Tor'gan's orb.",["sourceHash"]="80a839797b70ffe7f71827c4e35a307778d4112c811887b74a7903a6f89e6ee9",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[703]={["aftermath"]="Rigglefuzz prepared to cook and shared the recipe for future use.",["atomIDs"]={"703:description:1-50","703:description:53-92","703:description:95-154","703:description:159-202","703:description:205-242","703:description:247-293","703:description:296-355","703:objective:1-36"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"703:completion:1-47","703:completion:49-80","703:completion:85-145"},["opening"]="Rigglefuzz had sauce and everything else ready for his favorite barbecue. Only the wings themselves were missing from the proposed meal.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to collect four buzzard wings.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Rigglefuzz with the wings.",["sourceHash"]="767522c43b1c95fe268e2ed01cad765d39d379b8b0a3f9f8ab1f260052e134d5",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[704]={["aftermath"]="Ironband hoped diligence would reveal the link between artifacts and troggs, and promised that Agmond would be remembered.",["atomIDs"]={"704:description:1-80","704:description:83-169","704:description:172-269","704:description:274-318","704:description:321-379","704:objective:1-63"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"704:completion:1-10","704:completion:12-117","704:completion:122-172","704:completion:174-208","704:completion:210-233"},["opening"]="Agmond's last report troubled Ironband after news of his death. Ancient urns might have provoked the troggs, echoing an earlier discovery of idols.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather four urns for study.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the carved urns to Ironband.",["sourceHash"]="aa07e44a1316595a1ad5eeb1d5dadbdff6bbe4be962d904a1123d8432385536e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[705]={["atomIDs"]={"705:description:1-81","705:description:84-127","705:description:130-161","705:description:166-199","705:description:202-236","705:description:239-311","705:description:314-361","705:description:366-404","705:description:407-467","705:description:472-507","705:objective:1-50"},["opening"]="Rigglefuzz relied on flash bombs to survive among the Badlands' predators. Blue pearl powder from distant coastal clams was the ingredient running low.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather nine pearls from the Vile Reef.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the blue pearls to Rigglefuzz.",["sourceHash"]="e752b743577e6bb07649a956d1c48b6547773df81568c07deb9b8e71155119df",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[706]={["atomIDs"]={"706:description:1-114","706:description:116-200","706:description:205-354","706:description:356-411","706:description:413-494","706:objective:1-49"},["opening"]="Sigrun had learned a fiery weapon technique from his former master. A rare still-beating drake heart would let him demonstrate the enchantment.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover a heart from Lethlor's whelps.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the black drake's heart to Sigrun.",["sourceHash"]="202b1dc1b5b73bf3e0541fe62dc4c5a0cd00270864a73cb9a31b6dfcb7523883",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[707]={["atomIDs"]={"707:description:6-152","707:description:157-258","707:objective:1-75"},["opening"]="Ironband had requested assistance concerning another excavation, though Stormpike lacked the details. The working site in Loch Modan was the place to hear what legwork was needed.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to speak with Prospector Ironband at his excavation.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="9d73a125730f176e40e99dfae89121a86e23f9291da4d1e3ac821f296194d57f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[708]={["atomIDs"]={"708:description:1-167","708:description:172-233","708:description:236-266","708:description:271-308","708:objective:1-61"},["opening"]="Acid had pitted the metallic box recovered from a condor's stomach. A stamped engine number tied it to Ironforge's Siege Brigade.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take the box to the Hall of Arms.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the corroded box in Ironforge.",["sourceHash"]="d1d07fcabf987953077e41571ddc7477995a75c25fae9f9ed6e4b2bbc3423857",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[709]={["aftermath"]="Theldurin welcomed the find as a possible source of salvation, without explaining or resolving the feared threat.",["atomIDs"]={"709:description:17-44","709:description:47-54","709:description:57-63","709:description:68-139","709:description:142-231","709:description:236-241","709:description:246-261","709:description:269-278","709:description:281-325","709:description:328-340","709:description:343-382","709:description:387-432","709:description:435-507","709:objective:1-50"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"709:completion:1-23","709:completion:25-34","709:completion:36-55"},["opening"]="Theldurin feared a danger he refused to name. He sought an ancient tablet hidden in Uldaman, hoping knowledge could offer a means of resistance.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover the tablet from its ancient chest.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the tablet to Theldurin.",["sourceHash"]="46695c35c754b2ae9cd53721cb95cb9ebd9fd1d6ed44f5f701dbfb13d70dd7fc",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[710]={["atomIDs"]={"710:description:1-97","710:description:102-213","710:description:215-349","710:description:354-437","710:description:439-462","710:objective:1-77"},["opening"]="Lotwil's new shackles were meant to bind stronger elementals. Small fragments from lesser rock creatures would let him test spells and mechanical devices.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather ten small shards.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Lotwil with the stone samples.",["sourceHash"]="2125fb208eae6887745cfd2b4bde0de51e32d62f9290e8f32def91a6612a608a",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[711]={["atomIDs"]={"711:description:1-69","711:description:74-126","711:description:128-202","711:description:204-309","711:description:311-389","711:description:394-471","711:objective:1-61"},["opening"]="Lotwil's tests progressed from small fragments to heavier material. Larger rock elementals could supply slabs while he continued studying the first samples.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to bring three large slabs.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the slabs to Lotwil.",["sourceHash"]="968017b77784ebe709dfb943e4db998bdd3ccec99d7fb69651a3cae2fe957863",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[712]={["atomIDs"]={"712:description:1-136","712:description:138-229","712:description:234-354","712:description:359-408","712:description:410-467","712:objective:1-67"},["opening"]="Greater elementals carried the binding bracers Lotwil needed for comparison. He wanted five to gauge his own shackles and allow for misplaced samples.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather five rock-binding bracers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the bracers to Lotwil.",["sourceHash"]="6119bf66b21fa5bc164c957533ee2e9691da97c79104835a2c1d350ecb598df6",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[713]={["atomIDs"]={"713:description:1-110","713:description:115-203","713:description:205-276","713:description:281-426","713:description:431-489","713:description:491-506","713:objective:1-59"},["opening"]="Lotwil valued frost oil as coolant, lubricant and aid to enchantments. His shackles needed its capacity before a summoning could be safely restrained.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to obtain frost oil for the project.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the oil to Lotwil.",["sourceHash"]="421ee5a4ee161fce7754da60fb0951237db7cd5d51a71e82456ca4241af3d4b1",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[714]={["aftermath"]="Lotwil prepared to fit it into place, while conceding that finishing could still take considerably longer.",["atomIDs"]={"714:description:1-51","714:description:56-99","714:description:104-165","714:description:170-176","714:description:178-195","714:description:197-206","714:description:208-214","714:description:219-249","714:description:251-317","714:description:322-406","714:objective:1-57"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"714:completion:8-49","714:completion:54-63","714:completion:65-80","714:completion:82-92","714:completion:94-114","714:completion:116-149","714:completion:151-164","714:completion:166-251","714:completion:253-292","714:completion:294-301","714:completion:303-318","714:completion:320-344","714:completion:346-357"},["opening"]="The distracted inventor named one more small but crucial component. A gyrochronatom would bring his binding project closer to completion.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to obtain the missing mechanism.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Lotwil with the gyrochronatom.",["sourceHash"]="bf87c4ef5035262dd62334cfee13e14f3f5e0356d3869956ec137575ae8514bb",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[715]={["atomIDs"]={"715:description:1-94","715:description:96-209","715:description:214-321","715:description:326-423","715:description:425-496","715:objective:1-95"},["opening"]="Lucien worried about what Lotwil's completed invention might do. Healing and invisibility potions offered precautions while the larger experiment proceeded.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring Lucien both requested potions.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the potions to Lucien.",["sourceHash"]="de664236feabfe4a63f879f2a43fd77ce3698252abf98c88c019da9b77130357",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[716]={["atomIDs"]={"716:description:1-87","716:description:89-181","716:description:186-312","716:description:314-342","716:description:347-459","716:objective:1-75"},["opening"]="Lucien had used leftover stones to develop enchanted bracers. A smith's patterned bronze pair was needed to finish the protective work.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to obtain the bronze bracers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the patterned bracers to Lucien.",["sourceHash"]="a087c0e489a0ec0fd2040a796c0297347f97b29f62801908669a3c4b61c8e19d",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[717]={["aftermath"]="Garek declared the prisoners no longer a concern for the Kirin Tor and planned to report to Krasus.",["atomIDs"]={"717:description:1-105","717:description:107-260","717:description:265-372","717:description:374-446","717:description:457-493","717:objective:1-107","717:objective:112-187","717:objective:192-292"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"717:completion:1-73","717:completion:75-119","717:completion:121-152"},["opening"]="Garek no longer trusted the drakes' prison after the theft and new arrivals in Lethlor. The recovered sign could release its runestones and let the captives be confronted.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to release the drakes and return their bindings and sign.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Garek's assignment against Blacklash and Hematus.",["sourceHash"]="1d403236a428e8f3d95dc1d9bad3b05ba52c671166adad959edafb332dd800e6",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[718]={["atomIDs"]={"718:description:1-126","718:description:128-229","718:description:231-262","718:description:264-288","718:description:293-365","718:description:367-441","718:description:446-508","718:objective:1-45"},["opening"]="The hasty retreat from Uldaman left Sigrun's party without its equipment. Ogres had taken the weapons cart, leaving even hunting for food difficult.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to retrieve the missing supply crate.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the crate to Sigrun.",["sourceHash"]="5372f4aae751039cb4e2ac7cf09fecb56a85e6625caed32365e02d4356b4a7e8",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[719]={["atomIDs"]={"719:description:1-8","719:description:10-32","719:description:34-105","719:description:110-224","719:description:226-255","719:description:260-385","719:description:390-430","719:description:432-479","719:description:481-504","719:objective:1-90"},["opening"]="Ryedol barely escaped the Shadowforge attack on his dig. He believed Hammertoe dead and wanted supplies recovered, especially the lucky pick taken in the raid.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover Ryedol's missing pick.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the pick to Ryedol.",["sourceHash"]="76094c6bed9071db4faf7ddccb4916d21854e61239e3fb416c6ad37f2a7afe23",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[720]={["atomIDs"]={"720:description:1-54","720:description:59-67","720:description:70-98","720:description:100-109","720:description:112-122","720:objective:1-64"},["opening"]="A chalk message contradicted the worst report from the dig. Hammertoe named Uldaman as his destination and asked Ryedol to send help.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to bring Ryedol the news of survival.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} told Ryedol of Hammertoe's message.",["sourceHash"]="c13b11dcff0a21a88968188074fe302303eb1698895ec03ed332e824fb3f2a7a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[721]={["aftermath"]="Hammertoe was alive but coughing and weak when he received the visitor Ryedol sent.",["atomIDs"]={"721:description:1-20","721:description:22-55","721:description:60-214","721:description:219-313","721:description:315-377","721:description:382-491","721:objective:1-31"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"721:completion:1-4","721:completion:6-18","721:completion:20-40","721:completion:42-64","721:completion:69-83","721:completion:85-157","721:completion:159-165"},["opening"]="Ryedol feared Hammertoe's knowledge of titan excavations could strengthen Dark Iron golems. He suspected captivity rather than safety behind the surviving message.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to find Hammertoe inside Uldaman.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Hammertoe in the ruins.",["sourceHash"]="11f94624ec7178aca2de15483906c625e7c7ca2f78672a7df0fb876d4aa02f96",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[722]={["atomIDs"]={"722:description:1-14","722:description:16-25","722:description:27-58","722:description:63-93","722:description:95-116","722:description:118-127","722:description:129-150","722:description:152-161","722:description:166-187","722:description:189-208","722:description:210-228","722:description:230-251","722:description:253-278","722:description:280-289","722:description:292-332","722:description:334-352","722:description:354-362","722:description:364-379","722:description:384-460","722:description:462-476","722:description:478-503","722:objective:1-56"},["opening"]="The wounded prospector identified Deepshadow as the holder of his amulet. He feared it would lead the Dark Irons to scrolls useful for stronger golems.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover Hammertoe's amulet.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the amulet to Hammertoe.",["sourceHash"]="55301e94d63dab63c94ce04d0e4cfa40a4593fde9c83deee502640c9dc73bb8f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[723]={["aftermath"]="Ryedol received the object as his mentor's life's work and spoke of ensuring that his death would not be in vain.",["atomIDs"]={"723:description:1-94","723:description:99-114","723:description:116-135","723:description:137-158","723:description:160-189","723:description:191-249","723:description:251-260","723:description:262-319","723:description:321-367","723:description:369-375","723:objective:1-61"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"723:completion:1-19","723:completion:21-78","723:completion:80-122","723:completion:124-155","723:completion:157-189"},["opening"]="Hammertoe entrusted the amulet to a return journey to Ryedol. Protecting the scrolls and resisting the Shadowforge remained the purpose of his work.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to carry the amulet to Ryedol.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Hammertoe's amulet.",["sourceHash"]="6d84de879f0993531d86cf989e6a3e14bb1a7e22995d0ba851229b7251c5d2bf",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[724]={["aftermath"]="Karnik acknowledged Hammertoe's death but deferred mourning because of what the amulet placed at stake.",["atomIDs"]={"724:description:1-13","724:description:15-40","724:description:45-61","724:description:63-72","724:description:77-94","724:description:96-117","724:description:119-195","724:description:200-283","724:description:288-395","724:objective:1-57"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"724:completion:5-46","724:completion:48-113","724:completion:118-233","724:completion:238-288","724:completion:293-354"},["opening"]="Ryedol turned toward Hammertoe's fellow researcher in Ironforge. Karnik's part in the search for Uldaman artifacts made him the next keeper of the amulet.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to carry the amulet and news to Karnik.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered both to the historian.",["sourceHash"]="a5620376e313e588852d82b39f714e97a43b06cdc0280601aea638964ce94045",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[725]={["atomIDs"]={"725:description:1-55","725:description:57-126","725:description:128-162","725:description:167-235","725:description:237-347","725:description:349-365","725:objective:1-43"},["opening"]="Karnik sought authority for the next move and prepared a note for Belgrum. Meanwhile, he intended to consult Hammertoe's spirit about stopping the Shadowforge.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to take Karnik's note to Belgrum.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the note to the advisor.",["sourceHash"]="78d35b8169f360ee79547f7dc2cf11b2516bb05e5bbca3b410f5212b92048294",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[726]={["aftermath"]="Karnik identified Angor Fortress as the place to strike the enemy's base and hinder its work in Uldaman.",["atomIDs"]={"726:description:1-79","726:description:84-111","726:description:116-240","726:description:242-299","726:objective:1-26"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"726:completion:1-81","726:completion:86-101","726:completion:103-144","726:completion:149-250"},["opening"]="Belgrum's reading of the note produced a royal directive. Karnik was to act swiftly against the Shadowforge's Badlands operations.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to relay the king's authority to Karnik.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned with Belgrum's instruction.",["sourceHash"]="6fa53d2b139c297ba73f36a887982cef7e78541d70766ca0514a2f1102acae1d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[727]={["atomIDs"]={"727:description:1-22","727:description:25-39","727:description:42-59","727:description:64-120","727:description:123-129","727:description:131-147","727:description:149-183","727:description:186-217","727:description:220-243","727:description:246-269","727:description:274-295","727:description:298-349","727:description:352-403","727:description:406-436","727:description:438-456","727:objective:1-83"},["opening"]="The tablet had not answered enough of Theldurin's questions. He offered a sigil that would gain a copy of Yagyin's book from a secretive contact in Ironforge.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to show the sigil to Gerrig.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} presented the sign in the Forlorn Cavern.",["sourceHash"]="79d1c13d03ec36593a56bf2e37ac510265d352d3baf4c91523cac071108441a5",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[728]={["aftermath"]="Bel'dugur urged discretion because outsiders might oppose the order if they learned of it.",["atomIDs"]={"728:description:1-22","728:description:25-39","728:description:42-59","728:description:64-120","728:description:123-128","728:description:130-150","728:description:152-186","728:description:189-220","728:description:223-246","728:description:249-272","728:description:277-329","728:description:332-383","728:description:386-433","728:objective:1-67"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"728:completion:1-32","728:completion:34-100","728:completion:105-165","728:completion:170-195","728:completion:197-209","728:completion:211-222"},["opening"]="Theldurin named an alternative keeper of the old book in the Undercity. The same sigil was intended to pass its bearer as a member of the hidden order.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to present the sigil to Bel'dugur.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the sign to the keeper.",["sourceHash"]="e651e2c3d0694286a080f1e15ce260a56b46c06dcdaeffb13fff39ef9c503c89",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[729]={["atomIDs"]={"729:description:1-118","729:description:120-194","729:description:199-229","729:description:237-269","729:description:274-318","729:description:320-385","729:description:387-419","729:description:421-453","729:description:458-511","729:objective:1-47"},["opening"]="Hollee fled to Auberdine after golems rose at the excavation. Her celebrated mentor Remtravel seemed oblivious to the danger, leaving the apprentice desperate for someone to check on him south of town.",["pending"]="{actor} would check on Prospector Remtravel.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Prospector Remtravel at the southern excavation.",["sourceHash"]="7ecfde41549bee21251229f58ef877c8c0227fd728f4fdad992724f8bbe941c9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[730]={["atomIDs"]={"730:description:1-86","730:description:91-168","730:description:170-337","730:description:342-398","730:description:400-431","730:description:436-499","730:objective:1-70"},["opening"]="Greywhisker had heard nothing from the crew sent to Darkshore for weeks. He considered archaeology more than a hobby, with recent discoveries warning of a power threatening both continents, and feared for the missing team.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to seek signs of the excavation team in Auberdine.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the excavation-team inquiry with Archaeologist Hollee in Auberdine.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="81c328d87f624ee59ece1de46fc85967ff7f4adc30c427ca79933bd3405dce85",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[731]={["atomIDs"]={"731:description:1-18","731:description:20-55","731:description:57-71","731:description:76-104","731:description:106-137","731:description:139-167","731:description:169-193","731:description:195-282","731:description:287-353","731:description:355-368","731:description:370-426","731:description:431-451","731:objective:1-120"},["opening"]="Remtravel muddled his stone brush with a mysterious fossil, but insisted on searching. The find was meant to show the Explorers' League what his work had produced, and the distracted prospector needed protection during the hunt.",["pending"]="{actor} would protect Remtravel during his fossil search and report to Hollee.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Remtravel's protection assignment and returned to Archaeologist Hollee.",["sourceHash"]="f472a19b3b98092219d1659e3434dd69430e4546419dd02fb57f725f9442154b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[732]={["aftermath"]="Garek explained that Dark Irons created it to bind Deathwing's twin lieutenants Blacklash and Hematus.",["atomIDs"]={"732:description:1-59","732:description:61-93","732:description:95-204","732:description:209-341","732:description:346-464","732:description:466-506","732:objective:1-41"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"732:completion:1-44","732:completion:46-203"},["opening"]="Garek's undisclosed assignment came from Krasus. Before explaining more, he needed an earth-sign stolen by wandering ogres near Camp Boff.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover the stolen sign.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the sign to Garek.",["sourceHash"]="d2c0672c46f2ea8d79fd6afdc0e7eb8f441f1279b16d3e46767d1ab5a7a0375f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[733]={["aftermath"]="Sigrun considered it only a start until word came from Ironforge or the Explorers' League.",["atomIDs"]={"733:description:1-131","733:description:133-214","733:description:216-297","733:description:302-425","733:description:430-504","733:objective:1-39"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"733:completion:1-98","733:completion:103-174"},["opening"]="Sigrun needed material for defenses around the vulnerable camp. Scrap carried by local ogres might answer the need while aid from Ironforge remained uncertain.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather seven pieces of scrap metal.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the metal to Sigrun.",["sourceHash"]="3d3395cab9af7629ce68a2c22c1aec2f267e9cdeace171d46137971f16469b32",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[734]={["atomIDs"]={"734:description:1-21","734:description:26-97","734:description:102-124","734:description:126-141","734:description:143-167","734:objective:1-45"},["opening"]="Lotwil interrupted work on his shackles with another component request. Lucien was to provide the cog before the experiment could advance.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to ask Lucien for cog number five.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Lucien about the part.",["sourceHash"]="d8bdd3f40829b9b260ddd992bb9ad0c89020febc9ee8f78ae378de9b67384c82",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[735]={["atomIDs"]={"735:description:1-20","735:description:23-70","735:description:73-110","735:description:115-156","735:description:159-186","735:description:189-212","735:description:217-247","735:description:250-297","735:description:302-330","735:description:333-350","735:description:353-385","735:objective:1-72"},["opening"]="Gerrig offered an extra copy of the book to someone he took for an ally. Three written requirements replaced names he feared speaking aloud.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover the three items on Gerrig's note.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the required objects to Gerrig.",["sourceHash"]="79c1999561cebf8db06fe95509639583cb84445de6c1d71bdfeac5297fa956dc",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[736]={["atomIDs"]={"736:description:1-25","736:description:28-71","736:description:74-140","736:description:145-169","736:description:174-204","736:description:207-250","736:description:255-322","736:description:327-356","736:description:359-445","736:objective:1-73"},["opening"]="Bel'dugur assumed the request for the old digest meant founding another chapter of his order. He offered a copy for three powerful objects whose names he would only write, not speak.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather the items on Bel'dugur's note.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the required relics.",["sourceHash"]="3baa6c3ace54e6ebc8c8eda0b64db2354e4df1467098a649028a0c8b10c9b31e",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[737]={["aftermath"]="Theldurin welcomed renewed hope while continuing to fear what might rise to the surface.",["atomIDs"]={"737:description:1-30","737:description:33-79","737:description:82-122","737:description:129-158","737:description:163-188","737:objective:1-35"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"737:completion:1-11","737:completion:13-30","737:completion:35-67","737:completion:69-103","737:completion:105-131","737:completion:133-201","737:completion:206-253","737:completion:256-306","737:completion:311-354"},["opening"]="Gerrig released the digest with a warning to guard its contents. Theldurin awaited the knowledge he hoped would protect against the danger beneath.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to carry the book back to Theldurin.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Yagyin's book.",["sourceHash"]="52b9c81662dcb36c9ee4408d67a1ad14a91fbbeacb20fa59010d1499f946a892",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[738]={["aftermath"]="A broken, scavenged skeleton was identified as Agmond's remains.",["atomIDs"]={"738:description:1-90","738:description:93-154","738:description:157-206","738:description:211-321","738:description:324-359","738:objective:1-12"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"738:completion:1-56","738:completion:58-117"},["opening"]="Weeks without a report left Ironband uncertain about Agmond's fate. The southernmost Badlands dig beyond Angor was the last known place to search.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find the missing prospector.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the search for Agmond.",["sourceHash"]="aca15de7334feb131c9befc81e658d8de2d0a0a2136543583438e5d3a4d300d9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[739]={["aftermath"]="Ironband accepted the news of Agmond's death while remembering the prospector's strength.",["atomIDs"]={"739:description:1-35","739:description:38-137","739:description:142-158","739:description:163-258","739:description:263-298","739:objective:1-31","739:objective:36-67","739:objective:72-115"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"739:completion:1-26","739:completion:28-122","739:completion:124-214"},["opening"]="Bloody marks showed Agmond had crawled across rock and sand before dying. Beside his hand, a name in the sandstone identified the target of the next inquiry.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to confront Murdaloc and report to Ironband.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against Murdaloc and the bonesnappers.",["sourceHash"]="609be351ad08c2d4d584134c4f2050f68c4d7c153a130bc900c757ee7fd8e33c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[741]={["atomIDs"]={"741:description:1-92","741:description:94-142","741:description:147-234","741:objective:1-75"},["opening"]="Hollee would not leave Darkshore without Remtravel. Instead, she entrusted his mysterious fossil to a traveler bound for Greywhisker and the Explorers' League in Darnassus.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take the mysterious fossil to Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the mysterious fossil to Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker.",["sourceHash"]="ba3131308ddb3b8f76a236b95f6306656daffd3a907d487cf79f73837e35aa4d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[742]={["atomIDs"]={"742:description:1-29","742:description:32-64","742:description:69-146","742:description:149-251","742:description:254-317","742:description:320-469","742:objective:1-63"},["opening"]="Windstrider advertised a hunt beyond the Barrens, where two Horde outposts sought recruits. Senani at Splintertree was the contact for those willing to test themselves in Ashenvale.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to seek Senani's hunting guidance.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Senani.",["sourceHash"]="7e9249ad0e78b69bbab7dbd3894e9c957abd421d889eed0bac5116e5603b3c27",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[743]={["atomIDs"]={"743:description:1-49","743:description:51-81","743:description:86-209","743:description:214-309","743:description:311-368","743:description:373-463","743:objective:1-64"},["opening"]="Ruul offered the Windfury harpies as a measure of readiness for travel beyond Mulgore. Their nests lay along the southeastern mountain edges.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring eight harpy talons to Ruul.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the Windfury talons to Ruul.",["sourceHash"]="64b07b4f203acc0cd59fa13b39f1a25ca83ced57662de5dbdc556d6c8987def5",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[744]={["aftermath"]="Eyahn considered his work almost complete, with giving the headdress and witnessing the ceremony still ahead.",["atomIDs"]={"744:description:1-100","744:description:105-177","744:description:179-278","744:description:283-398","744:description:400-464","744:objective:1-100"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"744:completion:1-28","744:completion:33-84","744:completion:86-169"},["opening"]="Eyahn was tanning straps for his brother's ceremonial headdress. His part in the coming audience with Bloodhoof still required feathers he had no time to gather.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather six feathers of each color.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied the azure and bronze feathers.",["sourceHash"]="7e90a84cc8783d6598cc438e0128a50dd5aca8387ce5be1dfc79761f3a2eefe2",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[746]={["atomIDs"]={"746:description:1-56","746:description:59-181","746:description:186-283","746:description:288-322","746:description:325-426","746:objective:1-29","746:objective:34-97","746:objective:102-162"},["opening"]="Baine opposed the dwarven excavation as a violation of the land's teachings. He ordered their picks broken at a forge and brought back as evidence.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to break five prospectors' picks.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought five broken tools to Baine.",["sourceHash"]="427375889e6c991b1dea242df3df6ac515e07bc8632f43d3d8608408a2ef6235",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[749]={["aftermath"]="Mining Division markings identified the cargo as material destined for company processing.",["atomIDs"]={"749:description:1-38","749:description:40-109","749:description:111-216","749:description:221-334","749:description:336-407","749:description:412-486","749:objective:1-94"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"749:completion:1-67","749:completion:69-84","749:completion:86-216"},["opening"]="Morin's party burned a Venture Company caravan after an earlier battle cost two lives. Salvagers near the wreck suggested its abandoned crates survived.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to inspect a crate at the burned caravan.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} examined the caravan's supply crate.",["sourceHash"]="2472b9c3e3b2787c3545eb4df3521eacb0c6ed0ad7a67ce1b47d9a32695f3664",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[751]={["aftermath"]="Morin took the documents as confirmation that the company was exploiting Mulgore's resources.",["atomIDs"]={"751:description:1-140","751:description:142-219","751:description:224-335","751:objective:1-22","751:objective:24-78"},["bridge"]="Ore, minerals and documents inside the crate pointed beyond a single ruined wagon. Smoke and work in the eastern foothills gave the papers a place in the company's wider operation.",["bridgeFrom"]=749,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"751:completion:1-42","751:completion:44-92","751:completion:94-175"},["opening"]="The crate contained ore, minerals and a sheaf of documents. Work and smoke in the eastern foothills suggested the company's presence extended beyond the wreck.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring the company documents to Morin.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the documents to Morin.",["sourceHash"]="269b082a6a55a6941851a2921b85edd0f20044ca4597595b05eac3bca35880bb",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[761]={["atomIDs"]={"761:description:1-60","761:description:63-147","761:description:152-233","761:description:238-289","761:description:294-424","761:objective:1-69"},["opening"]="Harken treated swoop quills as evidence of a hunter's patience and skill. The birds ranged across Mulgore, difficult both to spot and to catch.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather eight trophy quills.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the swoop quills to Harken.",["sourceHash"]="3af1e4fd9644e89ac0120d0ba846e86b75525bdd48db7d26b244097579c1c1f8",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[762]={["aftermath"]="Belgrum planned to notify Karnik and send aid to recover the excavation site.",["atomIDs"]={"762:description:1-125","762:description:130-221","762:description:223-314","762:description:319-341","762:description:343-397","762:description:399-482","762:description:487-510","762:objective:1-104"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"762:completion:1-77","762:completion:79-119","762:completion:124-303","762:completion:305-320","762:completion:325-414"},["opening"]="Karnik named Ragnaros's ambassador as the overseer of Shadowforge artifact hunting. The casualties and danger to Ironforge demanded a strike at Angor's representative.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to confront Infernus and bring proof to Belgrum.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered proof of Infernus's defeat.",["sourceHash"]="a758654bcf56b2f376de9435a17482782aca4e62a820392bd2685a8f1ca4ac5e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[764]={["atomIDs"]={"764:description:1-40","764:description:42-87","764:description:89-104","764:description:106-163","764:description:165-254","764:description:259-289","764:description:291-404","764:description:406-479","764:objective:1-19","764:objective:21-45","764:objective:47-102"},["bridge"]="Morin read the growing workforce and equipment as signs of an expanding mine. The company's extraction in tauren lands now called for a direct response.",["bridgeFrom"]=751,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Morin linked the growing workforce and equipment to the company's expanding mine. He sought a forceful response to its extraction in tauren lands.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to confront the mine's workers and supervisors.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Morin's assignment at the company mine.",["sourceHash"]="ce4d0e000756ef3eba5024c94a6811ac1014fcb5787c80cf90a222ef79e593b7",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[765]={["aftermath"]="Morin planned to study the supervisor's papers for evidence of future company operations.",["atomIDs"]={"765:description:1-73","765:description:75-193","765:description:198-279","765:description:281-328","765:description:330-401","765:description:403-435","765:description:437-504","765:objective:1-96"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"765:completion:1-79","765:completion:81-192","765:completion:194-220","765:completion:222-252"},["opening"]="The caravan papers described plans to drive the tauren away. Morin identified Fizsprocket as their author and wanted his clipboard examined for further plans.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to confront Fizsprocket and recover his clipboard.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Fizsprocket's clipboard to Morin.",["sourceHash"]="3693db2505943a0c608a3ef03a71694558d3fe523773eaa16670ecfde840a9f6",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[766]={["aftermath"]="Maur expected the remedy to stop the infection and eventually cure it; recovery was still ahead.",["atomIDs"]={"766:description:1-82","766:description:84-156","766:description:161-281","766:description:283-329","766:description:331-476","766:description:481-510","766:objective:1-128"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"766:completion:1-18","766:completion:20-166","766:completion:168-195","766:completion:200-316","766:completion:321-344"},["opening"]="Maur recognized the strider from his grandfather's stories, but the bite was painfully his own. Four animal parts were needed to treat its infection.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather the ingredients for Maur's remedy.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Maur with all four remedy ingredients.",["sourceHash"]="8b1bd0e7ce521c71846b12932d7f7b11ad99b8cf028dd259263ab06c4daf87ff",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
